# 1v1, cloud locks to the PC (BENCH-253), round 24. Round 23 ran as PR #1018 (RAM-20 ram-learn: 19 of 25 held and are banked).
# Round 24 carries RAM-21, the known rammer (ram-known lines), on 16 robots: 9 that hold a ram-learn line on master are read
# on rkn (the ram-known line added), 7 that hold none on rlnrkn (both lines added). All are read in c and aa, so no A/A pad.
# Cloud read (Robocode 1.12.0, live turn time; c is master before the ram-learn lines were banked, aa its A/A copy), the
# list jar with both lines on all 16, 12 seeds from 64801, vs c / vs aa: +3.48 +- 0.32 / +3.57 +- 0.28 (A/A -0.09 +- 0.29).
#   Per robot vs c / vs aa:
#      Dreadnaught +6.3+-1.2 / +5.6+-1.3; MaxRisk +5.7+-1.3 / +6.7+-0.9; Bicephal +4.9+-1.5 / +3.3+-1.3
#      Fusion +4.4+-1.6 / +5.4+-1.1; Galaxy03 +4.3+-1.2 / +5.5+-1.6; RammingC +3.9+-1.5 / +4.1+-1.3
#      GrubbmThree +3.6+-0.9 / +3.3+-1.1; nanoPri +3.6+-1.4 / +3.7+-1.2; NanoDeath +3.4+-1.2 / +3.5+-1.1
#      DOSexe +2.9+-0.9 / +2.9+-0.6; Impact +2.7+-1.2 / +2.2+-1.3; Machete +2.5+-1.8 / +4.3+-2.6
#      PureAggression +2.3+-1.3 / +2.7+-1.0; Kowari +2.0+-1.1 / +2.1+-0.8; Hodur +1.4+-0.4 / +1.1+-0.3
#      Leopard +1.7+-0.9 / +0.6+-0.8 (with the first lock's 12 seeds, vs aa +0.8+-0.6 on 24)
#   What the ram-known line adds over the ram-learn line alone (the first lock, 16 close-range robots, 12 seeds 64501):
#      both lines against ram-learn alone +1.43 +- 0.56; both against c +2.63 +- 0.58. On every rammer at once the known
#      line loses (54 more robots, 18 seeds: -0.67 +- 0.36; URDOS -22, Sighup, Snezhok), so it is per robot only.
#   livematch  the released jar and BeepBoop 2.0 on the 31-robot panel at the live constant, read against live
#   lock       panel-locks.txt  c / aa / rkn / rlnrkn, 12 fresh seeds from 86600, --cpu-constant live, in work/pc-locks24
#              (earlier rounds' battles stay in work/pc-locks to -locks23)
#   gate       each robot judged on its own lever arm only (lock_prep.py --restrict); it keeps its line where the 95%
#              low end is above 0 (mode_table.py --margin 0).
# Leigh starts it once the PC is free (one card at a time, from master):
#   git checkout master && git pull
#   .\queue.ps1 run pc-locks --fresh        (or  ./queue.sh run pc-locks --fresh)
#   --fresh because round 23 left this plan's queue state marked complete; the new work directory and seeds mean no
#   battle is read back from an earlier round (and BENCH-272 refights any whose jar changed).
# One bench queue, RoboRumble workers at 0, 16 workers, truth log off. 600 lock battles (16 robots in c and aa, 9 in rkn, 7 in rlnrkn, 12 seeds),
# about 25 minutes with the live-match check. The prep step stops if any panel robot's jar is missing.
#
# Why it should win (the PC card rule of 2026-11-03):
#   - Per-opponent tailoring: each line names one robot; every other robot, team and melee play bit for bit as master
#     (ramKnowns() is empty on master and the switch is read in duels only).
#   - Diagnosis: RAM-2 confirms a rammer only after it has rammed us in two rounds, so rounds 1 and 2 of every battle are
#     fought at point-blank range. On the close-range robots those rounds cost 41.7 damage a round and are won 90% of the
#     time, against 30.0 and 99% once the escape plays. The line confirms the named robot at the first scan.
#   - Why per robot: the escape must suit the robot from the first round; where it does not (URDOS, Sighup, Snezhok) the
#     line costs points, so only robots that cleared 0 against both controls with the line on carry it.
#   - Why with ram-learn: alone the known line read level on the 16 (-0.35 +- 0.86), because the early escape rounds are
#     dodged with RAM-5's fixed aims; with the learned shot model on, the same rounds pay (+1.43 +- 0.56 over the model).
#   - Cost: about 3 more skipped turns a battle on the cloud (6.2 against 3.1); the lock's skip rule guards it on the PC.
# Stop rules (docs/bench/watch.md): the watcher's A/A rule needs 10 robots read in both c and aa; this lock reads 16, but
# the gate reads aa (multiarm.py prints aa against c), so no aa stop rule is set. The lock halts on 30 failed battles, an
# arm scoring nothing in 8, 60+ skipped turns a battle over the last 24 or no battle in 30 minutes. The live-match step
# stops the card if the PC no longer scores us and BeepBoop as live does (tools/live_match.py exit 3).
# ALERT opens an issue for Leigh on any stop.
# Bank: the owning cloud thread adds the gate's lines in a PR after this card's results PR. Nothing is released by the card.
set V = 3.24
set P = --parallel 16 --no-truth-log --failed-ok
set C = --skip-build --skip-fetch --rounds 35 --cpu-constant live --child-heap 2G
set W = work/pc-locks24
set OUT = ../docs/bench/local
set ALERT = lgriffin

prep | git checkout -q master && mkdir -p bisect work && (cd .. && mvn -q -DskipTests package) && cp ../hadur-robot/target/hadur117.Hadur_${V}.jar bisect/ && bash ./build-ablation.sh aa && python3 tools/lock_prep.py plans/locks-pick.tsv panel-locks.txt plans/pc-locks.arms ${W}-prep && bash ${W}-prep/build.sh && for a in rkn rlnrkn; do test -f bisect/hadur117.Hadur_${V}$a.jar || exit 1; done && bash tools/fetch_live_jar.sh && ./fetch-opponents.sh --set panel-r31.txt && ./fetch-opponents.sh --set livematch-bb.txt && test -f opponents/kc.mega.BeepBoop_2.0.jar && ./fetch-opponents.sh --set panel-locks.txt && for j in $(grep -v "^#" panel-locks.txt | cut -d"|" -f3); do test -f opponents/$j || { echo "missing jar $j"; exit 1; }; done && mvn -q compile

livematch | ./bench-top20.sh ${C} ${P} --set panel-r31.txt --seeds 2 --seed-base 21700 --arms plans/livematch.arms --out work/pc-livematch-rel-live --label pc-locks-livematch --shuffle-jobs && python3 tools/live_match.py work/pc-livematch-rel-live/arms.tsv --out ${OUT}/pc-locks24-livematch.md
  after: prep
  watch: field=1217
  stop: fails 30
  stop: dead 8
  stop: stall 30m

lock | ./bench-top20.sh ${C} ${P} --set panel-locks.txt --seeds 12 --seed-base 86600 --arms ${W}-prep/lock.arms --out ${W} --label pc-locks --shuffle-jobs
  after: livematch
  watch: field=1217
  stop: fails 30
  stop: dead 8
  stop: skips 60 over 24
  stop: stall 30m

gate | python3 ../data/tools/multiarm.py ${W}/arms.tsv --out ${OUT}/$(date +%Y-%m-%d)_pc-locks24-lock.md && python3 tools/lock_prep.py --restrict ${W}/arms.tsv ${W}-prep ${W}/arms-picked.tsv && python3 ../data/tools/mode_table.py ${W}/arms-picked.tsv --margin 0 --out-tsv ${OUT}/pc-locks24-lock-pick.tsv --out ${OUT}/$(date +%Y-%m-%d)_pc-locks24-lock-pick.md && python3 tools/per_robot.py ${W}/arms-picked.tsv --arms rln --out ${OUT}/$(date +%Y-%m-%d)_pc-locks24-lock-per-robot.md --out-tsv ${OUT}/pc-locks24-lock-per-robot.tsv
  after: lock

pr | bash tools/open_results_pr.sh claude/pc-locks24-results "1v1 cloud locks, round 24 (RAM-21 ram-known, 16 robots) on 12 fresh PC seeds" ${OUT}/pc-locks24-livematch.md ${OUT}/*_pc-locks24-*.md ${OUT}/pc-locks24-lock-per-robot.tsv $(find ${OUT} -maxdepth 1 -name 'pc-locks24-lock-pick.tsv' -size +0c)
  after: gate
